Z||000001||Seanh||05-08-2001||10:49 PM||||Well, Iv noticed this problem with a few Fiero owners I know. Apperently what is happening in the mojority of problem units is the power button is shorting out. I work on these every day, so it was nothing for me to do it. I took the top off the radio and just bypassed the power button so the radio is on all the time the car is on.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-08-2001||11:28 PM||||before you do that.... unhook the battery. These older GM radios sometimes get scrambled.<P>also read in my cave. I've seen a bunch now where the main terminals have cracked loose from the little circuit board. This can cause all sorts of wierd problems.||||reg||1
